Regression test for the RUST_LOG="" (set-but-empty) vs. unset bug — see
`resolve_filter_source` in `src/main.rs`. Uses `report --dry-run`: `report`
otherwise drives a real `cargo-llvm-cov` subprocess as of P1, and running
that live from inside this very `cargo test` process triggers a full
instrumented rebuild-and-retest of the whole suite (confirmed OOM). `--dry-run`
exercises the exact same code path — including this log line — without
shelling out to a real tool or touching the filesystem, so it's safe
regardless of what's on PATH or where trycmd runs it from.

```
$ RUST_LOG= jci-coverage report --dry-run
[..]INFO jci_coverage::report: report [..]
(dry run) would run: cargo llvm-cov --all-features --lcov --output-path coverage/lcov.info
(dry run) would write [..]coverage/lcov.info
(dry run) would run: cargo llvm-cov report --summary-only

```
